{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases","id":1091960,"title":"Dissonance Edge Cases","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-13T08:38:46-07:00","id":1091960,"title":"Dissonance Edge Cases","content":"I use Fate to give a Sleepwalker Electrokinesis. This merit is non-supernal, and is 100% Fallen (Supernatural) Phenomena.<br /> <br /> When that Sleepwalker runs around zapping people with lightning bolts, does Dissonance kick in? Does Quiescence? They aren't actually witnessing anything Supernal happening, but they <i>are</i> witnessing something obviously supernatural, and that supernatural effect's root source <i>was</i> Supernal Magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T08:56:06-07:00","id":1091967,"title":"","content":"I would say treat it as if the sleepwalker had the merit without magic as without magic one couldnt tell. no Dissonance, no Quiescence. I see arguments for the other way thought, maybe seeing somebody go emperor palatine on somebody causes enough disbelief to (small b) trigger Dissonance at a spell that by itself isnt obvious. I think this is firmly in the domain of &quot;whatever the ST decides&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T11:09:40-07:00","id":1092013,"title":"","content":"To be clear - the Sleepwalker is a Sleepwalker -before- they are given the electrokinesis? If that's the case, no I would not say Dissonance occurs. It's the same if you have a fetish, or if you turn someone into a claimed with magic; The resulting effects and supernatural powers do not cause dissonance - however if someone realized that you - the mage - used magic to grant that? Dissonance would probably kick in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T14:24:57-07:00","id":1092096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092013#post1092013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear - the Sleepwalker is a Sleepwalker -before- they are given the electrokinesis?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the assumption, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T17:36:46-07:00","id":1092167,"title":"","content":"The subject is now a Sleepwalker, and doesn't cause Dissonance on the spell that's affecting him.<br /> What's more, unless anyone else realises that these powers must have been granted by Magic (possibly a long shot, requiring either specialist supernatural knowledge or a predisposition to blame everything on Magic), they won't cause Dissonance or suffer Quiescence either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T17:48:29-07:00","id":1092170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092013#post1092013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear - the Sleepwalker is a Sleepwalker -before- they are given the electrokinesis? If that's the case, no I would not say Dissonance occurs. It's the same if you have a fetish, or if you turn someone into a claimed with magic; The resulting effects and supernatural powers do not cause dissonance - however if someone realized that you - the mage - used magic to grant that? Dissonance would probably kick in.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the fact that ephemeral beings created with spells can still be dispelled is reason/precedent enough to have Phenomenal supernatural effects generated through Supernal magic be counted as obvious manifestations of Supernal magic, particularly given that at the level we're talking about the greater danger is in the number of breaking points the powers in questions are going to cause to observing Sleepers; Dissonance all but requires both high Integrity and egregious witness quantities to overcome the Withstand of Patterning/Unraveling/Making/Unmaking magic and the only thing separating Quiescence from the usual outcome of mortal exposure to the supernatural is Abyssal Resonance and the potential recurrence of the breaking point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T18:37:30-07:00","id":1092180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092170#post1092170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like the fact that ephemeral beings created with spells can still be dispelled is reason/precedent enough to have Phenomenal supernatural effects generated through Supernal magic be counted as obvious manifestations of Supernal magic, particularly given that at the level we're talking about the greater danger is in the number of breaking points the powers in questions are going to cause to observing Sleepers; Dissonance all but requires both high Integrity and egregious witness quantities to overcome the Withstand of Patterning/Unraveling/Making/Unmaking magic and the only thing separating Quiescence from the usual outcome of mortal exposure to the supernatural is Abyssal Resonance and the potential recurrence of the breaking point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Quiescence also -forces- you to forget. With other supernatural events, your mind naturally chooses to forget it or it doesn't. A Sleeper who is aware of the supernatural can still remember the breaking point he experiences - but cannot look at a supernal effect and remember it as it was.<br /> <br /> My thoughts are that the electrokinesis, and anything created from it, are not subject to dissonance - in the same way that a ghost is not suddenly subject to dissonance just because you summoned it there. If they realized that you had called it to you with magic, however, that spell would be targeted by dissonance. In the same way, if someone realized you granted the subject a supernatural merit, <i>that</i> would be subject to dissonance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:42:41-07:00","id":1092193,"title":"","content":"Sleepwalkers do not cause dissonance, nor do they suffer from Quiescence. That would be sleepers.<br /> <br /> Granted, people who witness the sleepwalker would likely be sleepers...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7825,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","user":"Falcon777","date":". 05-13-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T19:57:40-07:00","id":1092197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092180#post1092180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">My thoughts are that the electrokinesis, and anything created from it, are not subject to dissonance - in the same way that a ghost is not suddenly subject to dissonance just because you summoned it there. If they realized that you had called it to you with magic, however, that spell would be targeted by dissonance. In the same way, if someone realized you granted the subject a supernatural merit, </span><i>that</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> would be subject to dissonance.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The sidebar on what the definition of &quot;obvious magic&quot; is bears remembering \u2014 a ghost manifesting is certainly clearly, openly supernatural and a Sleeper who is lucid and capable of putting two and two together re: spectral apparitions appearing out of thin air is by definition conscious and cognizant of that not being something that just happens \u2014 nothing about any facet of the Curse requires that a specific actor be intuited as responsible for the impossibility that confronts the Sleeper witness.<br /> <br /> It serves as a decent anti-shovelhead measure, but it also lends to the isolating effects of Awakened magic if its visibly fantastical products are more or less consistently kept to the shadows \u2014 a fetish or a Fated psychic or a constructed ghost need not be imperishable to be useful as a Paradox-free supernatural instrument.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T21:57:56-07:00","id":1092229,"title":"","content":"I actually did read that before considering. The thing I keep in mind with that however is that while yes, something supernatural is obviously magical, only supernal things are what actually are affected by dissonance and the Abyss. The curse strikes sleepers after obvious magic, but only &quot;Magic&quot; in the sense of mages. Sleepers don't deal with the curse when seeing obvious fallen magic. By this token, what's obvious must be the magic of the spell itself - not the magic of the individual or being affected by the spell.<br /> <br /> Take the ghost. Say I cast a spell to force a ghost to materialize. I have cast that spell - this will create dissonance in anyone who sees it, because by it's nature it's supernal. _I_ did that. If a ghost had materialized without it, it would not have this issue. But if I were to -command- a ghost with psychic domination to materialize, it would be an aftereffect of me casting that spell - but just because I had given him the command which leads to a sleeper seeing an obviously supernatural effect does not really mean that my mental compulsion over the ghost wavers if they do not recognize that I am, in fact, controlling the ghost. It's still obviously magic, but it's not my magic, and it's not supernal magic. Similarly, if I granted a spirit the ability to possess someone, I would not immediately assume that when the spirit did the spell granting it that ability would be subject to dissonance - even with the mortal a puppet in their own body. Because while its my spell giving it the ability to possess, the possession itself is not the spell - the granting of it is.<br /> <br /> In this case, you are granting a person something supernatural - but it's not Truth. Because it's not Truth, when Sleepers witness it they don't have to pit it against the Abyssal Lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T23:05:33-07:00","id":1092247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092229#post1092229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually did read that before considering. The thing I keep in mind with that however is that while yes, something supernatural is obviously magical, only supernal things are what actually are affected by dissonance and the Abyss. The curse strikes sleepers after obvious magic, but only &quot;Magic&quot; in the sense of mages. Sleepers don't deal with the curse when seeing obvious fallen magic. By this token, what's obvious must be the magic of the spell itself - not the magic of the individual or being affected by the spell.<br /> <br /> Take the ghost. Say I cast a spell to force a ghost to materialize. I have cast that spell - this will create dissonance in anyone who sees it, because by it's nature it's supernal. _I_ did that. If a ghost had materialized without it, it would not have this issue. But if I were to -command- a ghost with psychic domination to materialize, it would be an aftereffect of me casting that spell - but just because I had given him the command which leads to a sleeper seeing an obviously supernatural effect does not really mean that my mental compulsion over the ghost wavers if they do not recognize that I am, in fact, controlling the ghost. It's still obviously magic, but it's not my magic, and it's not supernal magic. Similarly, if I granted a spirit the ability to possess someone, I would not immediately assume that when the spirit did the spell granting it that ability would be subject to dissonance - even with the mortal a puppet in their own body. Because while its my spell giving it the ability to possess, the possession itself is not the spell - the granting of it is.<br /> <br /> In this case, you are granting a person something supernatural - but it's not Truth. Because it's not Truth, when Sleepers witness it they don't have to pit it against the Abyssal Lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two problems with this:<br /> <br /> 1. Dissonance and Quiescence occur for more than just Awakened spellcasting even though they aren't brought on by less concentrated forms of supernatural power \u2014 most notably Supernal and Abyssal beings and Verges. Further, the effects of Dissonance on ruins of the Time Before are more or less flush with the effects of Disbelief on Atlantean ruins in 1e; surely &quot;orphaned&quot; supernatural inhabitants of such ruins would have merited mention somewhere if they weren't subject to the same vulnerability to exposure as their homes and wards?<br /> <br /> 2. The example of mind-controlling a ghost into manifesting doesn't work as a point of comparison to outright giving someone an obvious supernatural power that they didn't have before \u2014 the effect of mind-controlling an invisible monster into revealing itself is not &quot;clearly, openly supernatural&quot; <i>without </i>the context of a controlling actor. By a similar token, the way ephemeral possession works means by definition anyone under spiritual control is not conscious or cognizant <i>at all</i>, much less specifically of the impossibility of what's happening \u2014 if the indwelling spirit spent Essence to heal its host body and other Sleepers witnessed the open wounds closing, meanwhile, that's an obvious supernatural effect that relies on sustained Awakened magic to happen and therefore ought to prompt the same risks as regular spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Again I must point out that the only thing this reading really does is cut down on the extent to which heavily-altered overt supernatural proxies are a viable way for Masters and Adepts to conduct their business relative to taking on apprentices and/or getting a familiar or three; high-level magic is often more durable than the average Integrity rating in isolation, and the ability to more comprehensively declare one's available resources is advantage enough without extending the Subtle Arcana's lowered susceptibility to the Curse from their purviews' reduced visibility to outright immunity to the usual consequences of those facets of their Mysteries that <i>would</i> be visible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:19:26-07:00","id":1092254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Dissonance and Quiescence occur for more than just Awakened spellcasting </div> </div> </div>Wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like the fact that ephemeral beings created with spells can still be dispelled is reason/precedent </div> </div> </div>Dispelled with supernal magic and they vanish, if you make a spirit and send it out to do stuff, it wont cause Dissonance or Quiescence on those who see its actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:34:01-07:00","id":1092257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092254#post1092254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dissonance does not only affect the spells of mages&quot; and &quot;Quiescence, like Dissonance, is not limited to the spells of mages&quot; are both direct quotes from the book that go on to specifically elaborate in the direction I'm referring to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:43:12-07:00","id":1092260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092257#post1092257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Dissonance does not only affect the spells of mages&quot; and &quot;Quiescence, like Dissonance, is not limited to the spells of mages&quot; are both direct quotes from the book that go on to specifically elaborate in the direction I'm referring to.</div> </div> </div> </div>They both happen when witnessing <i>Supernal</i> things, yes ok. But supernatural merits, ghosts and spirits arnt supernal themselves so dont cause them. There is no obvious supernal magic at work when they are doing their thing. (to sleepers at least, the spell will probably be obvious to a mage)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T00:48:12-07:00","id":1092261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092247#post1092247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Two problems with this:<br /> <br /> 1. Dissonance and Quiescence occur for more than just Awakened spellcasting even though they aren't brought on by less concentrated forms of supernatural power \u2014 most notably Supernal and Abyssal beings and Verges. Further, the effects of Dissonance on ruins of the Time Before are more or less flush with the effects of Disbelief on Atlantean ruins in 1e; surely &quot;orphaned&quot; supernatural inhabitants of such ruins would have merited mention somewhere if they weren't subject to the same vulnerability to exposure as their homes and wards?<br /> <br /> 2. The example of mind-controlling a ghost into manifesting doesn't work as a point of comparison to outright giving someone an obvious supernatural power that they didn't have before \u2014 the effect of mind-controlling an invisible monster into revealing itself is not &quot;clearly, openly supernatural&quot; <i>without </i>the context of a controlling actor. By a similar token, the way ephemeral possession works means by definition anyone under spiritual control is not conscious or cognizant <i>at all</i>, much less specifically of the impossibility of what's happening \u2014 if the indwelling spirit spent Essence to heal its host body and other Sleepers witnessed the open wounds closing, meanwhile, that's an obvious supernatural effect that relies on sustained Awakened magic to happen and therefore ought to prompt the same risks as regular spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Again I must point out that the only thing this reading really does is cut down on the extent to which heavily-altered overt supernatural proxies are a viable way for Masters and Adepts to conduct their business relative to taking on apprentices and/or getting a familiar or three; high-level magic is often more durable than the average Integrity rating in isolation, and the ability to more comprehensively declare one's available resources is advantage enough without extending the Subtle Arcana's lowered susceptibility to the Curse from their purviews' reduced visibility to outright immunity to the usual consequences of those facets of their Mysteries that <i>would</i> be visible.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Dissonance effects anything Supernal. It does not actually affect the Abyss. Verges are explicitly immune to Dissonance, and in fact prevent spells cast in them from being subject to them (assuming they are natural - Demenses are very much not immune to Dissonance). In this, the question is whether or not Dissonance is a factor to the effects. As far as the ruins of the Time before, I'll be honest - I'm not exactly sure what your bringing to the table in this part of the discussion or what your referencing so it's hard for me to understand the point you are trying to make with that reference.<br /> <br /> 2) Fair point on the possession bit basically being something the mortal can't notice (though I don't agree with the essence-to-heal bit causing dissonance), so I will address the issue with the comparison to using Mind to create the supernatural effect. The problem here, is that to the mortal there is something supernaturally occuring and obviously supernaturally occuring in both instances. In both instances, the mortal does NOT know or sense the mage's part in this play. In both situations, the Sleepers do not witness &quot;Obvious Supernal Magic&quot; - they simply witness obvious magic. In both cases they see a supernatural effect, but it is not the mage's supernatural effect - even though the mage's supernatural effect is the reason they are seeing the effect they do see. Because it is not the mage's effect that they witness, it is not the mage's spell that would be the target of dissonance. Because the effect that they DO witness is not a viable option for dissonance, then dissonance should not be an issue. Yes - the major difference is in this case the mage is granting a gun, rather than telling a person to fire it. But in both cases, the person shooting the gun is not the mage.<br /> <br /> I get and understand that this particular reading doesn't really make much of a difference in the long run. Dissonance takes time, and really you are going to need to get 6 successes on that dissonace roll at the end of the scene to even touch a person's Fate Spell. This discussion is fairly academic. I still enjoy having it though, because as small a change as that is, it does alter methodologies of many mages - even if only slightly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T02:04:10-07:00","id":1092276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Falcon777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092193#post1092193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleepwalkers do not cause dissonance, nor do they suffer from Quiescence. That would be sleepers.<br /> <br /> Granted, people who witness the sleepwalker would likely be sleepers...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the assumption is that neo-Palpatine is running through Times Square shooting off Force Lightning at random in front of truckloads of Sleepers, sorry for not clarifying.<br /> <br /> For the purposes of the exercise we're ignoring other external factors that would interfere and just talking about The Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T02:21:17-07:00","id":1092278,"title":"","content":"They'd still probably suffer from a standard Breaking Point. It's a pretty big shift in one's life, just finding it out, and if you're blasting people throughout Times Square your 'the worst thing I've ever done' meter is going to get a few clicks.<br /> <br /> I have to ask, is the target aware a Mage is doing this? Or did they just plink it on him?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T02:33:48-07:00","id":1092279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092278#post1092278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They'd still probably suffer from a standard Breaking Point. It's a pretty big shift in one's life, just finding it out, and if you're blasting people throughout Times Square your 'the worst thing I've ever done' meter is going to get a few clicks.<br /> <br /> I have to ask, is the target aware a Mage is doing this? Or did they just plink it on him?</div> </div> </div> </div>We can assume neo-Palpatine is complicit.<br /> <br /> Really the focus is: &quot;Do all the Sleepers seeing this cause Dissonance? And are they forced to forget because of the Curse? Or is it just something they <i>might</i> forget like when seeing any other non-supernal, supernatural phenomena?&quot;<br /> <br /> The examples on the previous page are just as valid: Fetishes are Fallen. If I throw a spirit into a fetish and use it to start chucking fireballs at witchhunters, does The Curse intervene?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T14:54:23-07:00","id":1092517,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that supernatural things that are not directly caused by the Supernal are treated like other supernatural phenomena: likely to be forgotten or justified away, but not because of Quiesence. So fetishes used to cast fireballs would likely be explained away as a specialized flamethrower, but the Curse isn't going to be what causes people to forget, just normal human behavior. The same would be for any supernatural ability granted by a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:37:14-07:00","id":1092546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092260#post1092260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They both happen when witnessing <i>Supernal</i> things, yes ok. But supernatural merits, ghosts and spirits arnt supernal themselves so dont cause them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. I said this in the part of the sentence immediately following the snippet you &quot;Wrong&quot;ed at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092261#post1092261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Dissonance effects anything Supernal. It does not actually affect the Abyss. Verges are explicitly immune to Dissonance, and in fact prevent spells cast in them from being subject to them (assuming they are natural - Demenses are very much not immune to Dissonance). In this, the question is whether or not Dissonance is a factor to the effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking solely about the effects of Dissonance \u2014 I brought up the fact that both Dissonance and Quiescence <i>occur</i> to highlight specifically that facet of the problem, because the larger-scale implications of the decision to treat derived supernatural effects as valid or invalid subjects for the triggering of the Sleeping Curse include whether or not such effects serve as a potential long-term source of Abyssal Resonance; a fetish made with Awakened magic has a different impact on a setting if its public use is a beacon for gulmoth whose mere memory is an obfuscated source of madness and unreality than if it's just as threatening to human sanity as a similar fetish made with the relevant werewolf rite. (The flip side of this is that it's easier for Scelesti to wreak havoc by these methods, which ties back into that methodology question a bit.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the ruins of the Time before, I'll be honest - I'm not exactly sure what your bringing to the table in this part of the discussion or what your referencing so it's hard for me to understand the point you are trying to make with that reference. </div> </div> </div>Supernatural things regularly live in the ruins of the Time Before. Those ruins prompt the same responses in Sleepers as Awakened magic does and are subject to the same erosion (there's a sidebar on it in the Neolithic chapter of Dark Eras addressing the gradual disappearance of the bizarre structures common to that age). If those residents (who can be assumed to generally not depend upon the magical nature of the ruins for their continued existence) were not also sources of Quiescence and/or Dissonance, I feel that would have merited at least a token mention as a common story hook or at least a thing to be covered as a matter of why they don't happen with some regularity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the effect that they DO witness is not a viable option for dissonance, then dissonance should not be an issue. Yes - the major difference is in this case the mage is granting a gun, rather than telling a person to fire it. But in both cases, the person shooting the gun is not the mage. </div> </div> </div>My point of contention is more that, if Awakened spellcraft was necessary for the person to even have the gun in the first place, and the gun is obviously supernatural, then the gun ought to be subject to the same supernatural entropy that starts to break down the framework that was used to directly force a spirit into material form. I figure Awakened magic being the only common form that consistently risks this degradation just means that things that wouldn't be there without Awakened magic are a close enough referent to the spells that facilitate them happening in the first place \u2014 a ghost mind-controlled into manifesting could have manifested with or without the spell, but a Fate-born electrokinetic couldn't manipulate electricity without the spell, and a bow that shoots moonbeams by drawing on the power of a bound Lune doesn't happen without the binding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T20:17:59-07:00","id":1092643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092546#post1092546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. I said this in the part of the sentence immediately following the snippet you &quot;Wrong&quot;ed at.<br /> <br /> I wasn't talking solely about the effects of Dissonance \u2014 I brought up the fact that both Dissonance and Quiescence <i>occur</i> to highlight specifically that facet of the problem, because the larger-scale implications of the decision to treat derived supernatural effects as valid or invalid subjects for the triggering of the Sleeping Curse include whether or not such effects serve as a potential long-term source of Abyssal Resonance; a fetish made with Awakened magic has a different impact on a setting if its public use is a beacon for gulmoth whose mere memory is an obfuscated source of madness and unreality than if it's just as threatening to human sanity as a similar fetish made with the relevant werewolf rite. (The flip side of this is that it's easier for Scelesti to wreak havoc by these methods, which ties back into that methodology question a bit.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand this. But in this, the question is less about Quiescence and more about Dissonance. Two similar themes, but two different phenomena.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092546#post1092546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernatural things regularly live in the ruins of the Time Before. Those ruins prompt the same responses in Sleepers as Awakened magic does and are subject to the same erosion (there's a sidebar on it in the Neolithic chapter of Dark Eras addressing the gradual disappearance of the bizarre structures common to that age). If those residents (who can be assumed to generally not depend upon the magical nature of the ruins for their continued existence) were not also sources of Quiescence and/or Dissonance, I feel that would have merited at least a token mention as a common story hook or at least a thing to be covered as a matter of why they don't happen with some regularity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see. Problem is - I think in order for them to get any kind of mention, they'd have to mention the ruins of the time before in second edition to begin with. That they were not mentioned does not support or dissuade any discussion. They are literally an element that does not exist to prove a point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092546#post1092546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point of contention is more that, if Awakened spellcraft was necessary for the person to even have the gun in the first place, and the gun is obviously supernatural, then the gun ought to be subject to the same supernatural entropy that starts to break down the framework that was used to directly force a spirit into material form. I figure Awakened magic being the only common form that consistently risks this degradation just means that things that wouldn't be there without Awakened magic are a close enough referent to the spells that facilitate them happening in the first place \u2014 a ghost mind-controlled into manifesting could have manifested with or without the spell, but a Fate-born electrokinetic couldn't manipulate electricity without the spell, and a bow that shoots moonbeams by drawing on the power of a bound Lune doesn't happen without the binding.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems like a personally reasonable thought. My thoughts, however, are that just because something is caused by something doesn't mean that the cause has the same properties as the tools used to create it. What I mean is, just because a Supernal spell grants a supernatural ability, doesn't mean that those supernatural abilities are then inherently Supernal by proxie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T21:09:30-07:00","id":1092650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092643#post1092643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand this. But in this, the question is less about Quiescence and more about Dissonance. Two similar themes, but two different phenomena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem being that they're two different phenomena that are inherently tied together \u2014 if a Sleeper provokes Dissonance, they suffer Quiescence and have their ability to apply greater Dissonance threatened by subsequent disturbance of the patched-over memory of the supernatural occurrence. If an obvious supernatural phenomenon doesn't burrow into a Sleeper's mind and force them to pretend it they weren't witness to an obvious supernatural phenomenon, then it is not the sort of obvious supernatural phenomenon that provokes the degenerative unreality peculiar to Mage-specific forces. One doesn't happen without the other because they both have the same trigger conditions, and the one lessens the threat of the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I see. Problem is - I think in order for them to get any kind of mention, they'd have to mention the ruins of the time before in second edition to begin with. </div> </div> </div>And they did \u2014 look at the corebook on pages 243 and 244.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That seems like a personally reasonable thought. My thoughts, however, are that just because something is caused by something doesn't mean that the cause has the same properties as the tools used to create it. What I mean is, just because a Supernal spell grants a supernatural ability, doesn't mean that those supernatural abilities are then inherently Supernal by proxie. </div> </div> </div>My view is generally that engineering supernatural proxies whose powers aren't subject to the vulnerabilities of Supernal magic works best as the domain of archmages and god-botherers for anything that isn't a massive/concerted effort with at least one substantial Mystery built into the process \u2014 a Supernal spell that grants an obvious supernatural ability should not be completely immune to what little vulnerability it has to Dissonance just because its effects are most obvious at the shortest possible remove from the spell itself, I feel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T22:45:40-07:00","id":1092667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092650#post1092650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem being that they're two different phenomena that are inherently tied together \u2014 if a Sleeper provokes Dissonance, they suffer Quiescence and have their ability to apply greater Dissonance threatened by subsequent disturbance of the patched-over memory of the supernatural occurrence. If an obvious supernatural phenomenon doesn't burrow into a Sleeper's mind and force them to pretend it they weren't witness to an obvious supernatural phenomenon, then it is not the sort of obvious supernatural phenomenon that provokes the degenerative unreality peculiar to Mage-specific forces. One doesn't happen without the other because they both have the same trigger conditions, and the one lessens the threat of the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree: You can have Quiescence without Dissonance, namely when dealing with Emanations and natural Verges. It is likely true however that you cannot have Dissonance without Quiescence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092650#post1092650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they did \u2014 look at the corebook on pages 243 and 244.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough - a mention. But that's an abbreviated substance designed to state that that's still part of the game and what they are - it's not the complete reference work for what will and will not be mentioned in regards to it when it does come up more completely written out. It still doesn't really provide much substance to back the case - I mean, I could argue that if they thought that the supernatural merits would be subject to dissonance it'd have warranted a mention in the spell itself or in any reference to granting non-supernal powers; I am not, because it doesn't really help my case it just states they didn't mention it - which is why this discussion is even possible <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092650#post1092650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My view is generally that engineering supernatural proxies whose powers aren't subject to the vulnerabilities of Supernal magic works best as the domain of archmages and god-botherers for anything that isn't a massive/concerted effort with at least one substantial Mystery built into the process \u2014 a Supernal spell that grants an obvious supernatural ability should not be completely immune to what little vulnerability it has to Dissonance just because its effects are most obvious at the shortest possible remove from the spell itself, I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am looking at it slightly differently. The reason this kind of effect isn't an archmage level effect is because you aren't actually changing the template - what you are doing is taking the possibility that an individual might have a supernatural merit and making it so - at least for a time. If the effect they had were then subject to dissonance, it would actually suggest that the spell changed something -impossible- in the Sleepwalker, rather than changing something that was.<br /> <br /> Looking at this in another way: In this event, the spell is allowing the mage to either granting the Sleepwalker electrokinesis - but that same effect can also increase the Sleepwalkers dots in it if they already have it, or decrease it. Say that you opt to increase the electrokinesis from what they already have - electrokinesis 2 becomes 4 (In this theoretical example, the contrast - the sleepwalker who didn't have electrokinesis - was raised from 0 to 2). The Sleepwalker uses their abilities - obviously supernatural, only now increased. Perhaps they don't even use their new higher level abilities - they are using their default level 2. Would you still say that these powers were suddenly subject to dissonance, even though all you've done is increase the power of their capability to do so? In both circumstances, the same spell has been used - the same effect - adding 'x' amount of electrokinesis' - has been applied, and the Sleepers are all witnessing the exact same circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":". 05-15-2017, 01:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T00:12:47-07:00","id":1092682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092667#post1092667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree: You can have Quiescence without Dissonance, namely when dealing with Emanations and natural Verges.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absent future details about the Scelesti, you can have neither without Sleepers, who are generally light on the ground in Verges and moreso in Emanations. Natural Supernal manifestations fit into that &quot;Mysteries and god-botherers&quot; subset that I have little problem with \u2014 if you're exploiting the story-rich vein of tying a Sleepwalker proxy's power to a materialization of Supernal principles as vast as the likes of Yggdrasil or the Mists, you've got a narrative hook that justifies a lower attract-rate for the Abyss out in the wild.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the effect they had were then subject to dissonance, it would actually suggest that the spell changed something -impossible- in the Sleepwalker, rather than changing something that was. </div> </div> </div>The entire basis for the Curse kicking in is founded in the capacity for a Sleeper to observe an effect and think, &quot;This shouldn't be happening&quot; and edit their recollection of the scene toward a mundane version of events \u2014 the fact that Sleepwalkers <i>can have</i> supernatural powers doesn't change the fact that people don't control arcs of electricity with their bare hands any more than it immunizes Sleeper witnesses to the mundane breaking point a wholly Phenomenonal instance of that power would precipitate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Looking at this in another way: [\u2026] Would you still say that these powers were suddenly subject to dissonance, even though all you've done is increase the power of their capability to do so? In both circumstances, the same spell has been used - the same effect - adding 'x' amount of electrokinesis' - has been applied, and the Sleepers are all witnessing the exact same circumstances. </div> </div> </div>Let's set aside the fact that neither Electrokinesis 2 nor Electrokinesis 4 are things that mechanically exist and that strengthening an existing Merit is a different effect of Forge Destiny than granting an entirely new power to a target \u2014 the only unique benefit a higher level of Electrokinesis grants to an established electrokinetic is both arguably the most obvious form of the power and something that they couldn't accomplish without the spell; this draws a distinction between using the power that you only have because of the spell and using the power that you already had.<br /> <br /> Which makes the importance of empowering folks with obvious magic matter to your Wisdom rather than simply firing off the spell and having to pay no more mind to it than you would a regular supernatural being with a sympathetic connection to you and encourages Suspicious Empowering Character behavior from Scelesti who approach from that angle \u2014 I feel it opens more stories than it closes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T10:56:45-07:00","id":1092868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092682#post1092682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absent future details about the Scelesti, you can have neither without Sleepers, who are generally light on the ground in Verges and moreso in Emanations. Natural Supernal manifestations fit into that &quot;Mysteries and god-botherers&quot; subset that I have little problem with \u2014 if you're exploiting the story-rich vein of tying a Sleepwalker proxy's power to a materialization of Supernal principles as vast as the likes of Yggdrasil or the Mists, you've got a narrative hook that justifies a lower attract-rate for the Abyss out in the wild.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also get Quiescence without Dissonance when dealing with the Mad. The point here being it does not take an ancient god being to cause that effect - they are two different occurences which do not necessarily need to exist without the other. They are <i>likely</i> to exist together, but are not <i>needed</i> together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092682#post1092682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The entire basis for the Curse kicking in is founded in the capacity for a Sleeper to observe an effect and think, &quot;This shouldn't be happening&quot; and edit their recollection of the scene toward a mundane version of events \u2014 the fact that Sleepwalkers <i>can have</i> supernatural powers doesn't change the fact that people don't control arcs of electricity with their bare hands any more than it immunizes Sleeper witnesses to the mundane breaking point a wholly Phenomenonal instance of that power would precipitate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The entire basis for the Curse is that Sleepers cannot percieve the Truth because they have a shard of the Lie inside of them. Here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 299</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">When a Sleeper struggles with the non-choice she\u2019s been given by reality, it creates internal conflict, and that cycles back into the system. This conflict, this discord between what can and can\u2019t be real, degrades not just her own soul and mind, but also <b>symbols of the Supernal when she is exposed to them</b>. The Awakened call it Dissonance, and it is the brutal aftereffect of the Curse on the magics they attempt to create. Dissonance does not only affect the spells of mages, but any <b>exposure</b> to the <b>Supernal.</b> Worse, it makes Abyssal entities stronger.<br /> <br /> At the end of a scene in which a Sleeper<b> witnesses obvious Supernal magic</b>, roll her Integrity as a dice pool, Withstood by the spell\u2019s dots, the Rank of a Supernal entity, or a number set by the Storyteller for other magical phenomena. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphathis mine. I emphathize this because of these points - the electrokinesis is not a Symbol of the Supernal in the way the spell is. The witnesses here are not exposed the to Supernal (the Sleepwalker is, which is why I asked if the Sleepwalker was a Sleeper prior). The Witnesses are not witnessing obvious -supernal- magic; Just the obviously supernatural.<br /> <br /> As an obserbance - on the flipside to this, is that if a person with a Legacy that had Forge Destiny as an Attainment, that person shooting out electrokinesis would not have the properties of the attainment which makes people not suffer breaking points when they see it. Because they are not seeing the attainment, but rather the person shooting out the supernatural merits, people still see that as 'supernatural'.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092682#post1092682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's set aside the fact that neither Electrokinesis 2 nor Electrokinesis 4 are things that mechanically exist and that strengthening an existing Merit is a different effect of Forge Destiny than granting an entirely new power to a target \u2014 the only unique benefit a higher level of Electrokinesis grants to an established electrokinetic is both arguably the most obvious form of the power and something that they couldn't accomplish without the spell; this draws a distinction between using the power that you only have because of the spell and using the power that you already had.<br /> <br /> Which makes the importance of empowering folks with obvious magic matter to your Wisdom rather than simply firing off the spell and having to pay no more mind to it than you would a regular supernatural being with a sympathetic connection to you and encourages Suspicious Empowering Character behavior from Scelesti who approach from that angle \u2014 I feel it opens more stories than it closes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Electrokinesis 3 and 5 then. (This might actually have been an easier discussion if we forget the specific electrokinesis and point to -any- obvious use of such supernatural powers &gt;.&gt; Telekinesis would have worked fine in my example and not strayed from the point.) My point here is that - to the Sleepers witnessing the magic - they are witnessing the same thing, challenging the same things that cannot be. They are not challenging &quot;you cannot give people powers by altering the coarse of destiny&quot; - instead they are challenging &quot;you cannot throw lightning&quot;. The Supernal Symbol which was used should have no chance of erosion, because they have no chance of exposure to it... unless of course the Sleepwalker goes to his friends and says &quot;This cool guy in a cloak granted me the power to do THIS.&quot; (Because at that point the Dissonance has a valid target)<br /> <br /> I don't at all argue that empowering folks with obvious magic - bolstering or otherwise - matters to your Wisdom. The fact that that person is running around the street throwing electroballs means the person with fate magic -fucked up-. Having a bunch of people remembering someone shooting electrokinesis is such a huge breach of the Veil, bound to grab attention from damn near everything with a vested interest in not having that broken - that opens stories as well. From whatever direction you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T22:53:14-07:00","id":1093116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1092868#post1092868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also get Quiescence without Dissonance when dealing with the Mad.<br /> [\u2026]<br /> The entire basis for the Curse is that Sleepers cannot percieve the Truth because they have a shard of the Lie inside of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize that my bringing up the ruins of the Time Before as a referent to their inhabitants' general lack of isolated encounters with the mortal populace may have distracted from this, but I feel it bears reminding that this discussion is about Dissonance and Quiescence <i>as they relate to spells and their effects</i>. Dissonance does not occur for a spell without also prompting Quiescence, and with the exception of (what is technically one of multiple possible readings of the workings of) spells cast in an uncommon circumstance that expressly cannot be directly made by a Traveler's power alone,* a spell does not prompt Quiescence without risking Dissonance; the trigger criteria are identical for both facets of the Curse as they relate to a spell.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Emanation Realms and natural Verges may not be subject to Dissonance, but Supernal beings are, and the way the passage is written can be taken as either a wholesale immunity of spells cast within the area to Dissonance regardless of where they go afterward or an extension of the preceding lines' description of how spells that remain within the area benefit; I personally favor the former interpretation because developing sympathy to a unique otherworldly locale for the sake of getting special benefits to a spell appeals to me, but the significance of that kind of real-estate also seems to me to be something that should be of greater general interest to Masters than Apprentices rather than roughly equivalent \u2014 Dissonance is of greatest danger to the enduring products of high-level magic, while the more fragile nudges of elementary Gnosis can usually be attempted anew without difficulty.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Emphathis mine. I emphathize this because of these points - the electrokinesis is not a Symbol of the Supernal in the way the spell is. The witnesses here are not exposed the to Supernal (the Sleepwalker is, which is why I asked if the Sleepwalker was a Sleeper prior). The Witnesses are not witnessing obvious -supernal- magic; Just the obviously supernatural. </div> </div> </div>Your emphasis still runs afoul of the fact that obvious magic is defined by being &quot;clearly, openly supernatural <i>in effect</i>&quot; and the effect of the spell is &quot;this guy can now shoot lightning.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point here is that - to the Sleepers witnessing the magic - they are witnessing the same thing, challenging the same things that cannot be. They are not challenging &quot;you cannot give people powers by altering the coarse of destiny&quot; - instead they are challenging &quot;you cannot throw lightning&quot;. </div> </div> </div>We again come to the problem of the vast majority of the Subtle Arcana's purviews being invisible to Sleepers anyway \u2014 overt applications of those principles should not be immune to the degenerative effects Awakened magic has on reality solely through the use of occult phenomena when those effects can be better avoided by keeping to the natural tendencies of those beings toward silence and secrecy in the mortal sphere.<br /> <br /> My opinion that there's no Claim or Resurrection in Mage 2e's listing of Invisible Entity mechanics is founded in the same principle (wordcount notwithstanding) \u2014 Awakened magic oughtn't be able to outright create shortcuts past its own limitations as a direct exercise of Awakened magic without special considerations of the sort that mages tend to go out of their way for; unique Yantras and the gifts of spiritual diplomacy ought to matter more than raw occult power in a connected setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Supernal Symbol which was used should have no chance of erosion, because they have no chance of exposure to it... unless of course the Sleepwalker goes to his friends and says &quot;This cool guy in a cloak granted me the power to do THIS.&quot; (Because at that point the Dissonance has a valid target) </div> </div> </div>And the problem <i>here</i> is that the Sleepwalker's friends are under no compulsion to believe him and Dissonance does not &quot;target&quot; mages directly. A rat with gills challenges &quot;rats don't have gills&quot; rather than &quot;you cannot give mammals the features of fish&quot; and liquid diamonds challenge &quot;diamonds are not liquid at room temperature&quot; rather than &quot;you can't cold-melt diamonds.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't at all argue that empowering folks with obvious magic - bolstering or otherwise - matters to your Wisdom. The fact that that person is running around the street throwing electroballs means the person with fate magic -fucked up-. Having a bunch of people remembering someone shooting electrokinesis is such a huge breach of the Veil, bound to grab attention from damn near everything with a vested interest in not having that broken - that opens stories as well. From whatever direction you like. </div> </div> </div>The problem with this is that Quiescence is the nearest the setting gives to a consistent lasting threat out of this, given that spell control means the moment word gets back to you about your rogue agent you their power can be made to stop working unless you specifically cut yourself off from the ability to do so \u2014 memories can be altered and records can be lost, but the wound Quiescence forms around only stops being a potential source of Abyssal attraction if it's retroactively undone.<br /> <br /> Also, the Precept of Secrecy doesn't mean much in relation to what a Sleepwalker does, seeing as the Veil is a Mage Rule For Mages about how to conduct themselves in relation to talking and working shop around non-mages \u2014 it's nothing to do with whether there's a magical effect going around bedeviling the local Sleepers' Integrity ratings on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T00:11:34-07:00","id":1093135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1093116#post1093116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize that my bringing up the ruins of the Time Before as a referent to their inhabitants' general lack of isolated encounters with the mortal populace may have distracted from this, but I feel it bears reminding that this discussion is about Dissonance and Quiescence <i>as they relate to spells and their effects</i>. [...]</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough - getting off track. For the sake of ease and everyone's mind, I'm going to try address what I feel is most important to make it easier on both of us; If, however, you feel I should answer something that I choose not to, please let me know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1093116#post1093116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your emphasis still runs afoul of the fact that obvious magic is defined by being &quot;clearly, openly supernatural <i>in effect</i>&quot; and the effect of the spell is &quot;this guy can now shoot lightning.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Obvious magic defines that the <i>spell</i> must be clearly and openly supernatural in effect. My emphasis is based around that the Sleepers cannot perceive the spell at all in this scenario. They do not see &quot;He gained the ability to manipulate electricity&quot; they see &quot;He is manipulating electricity.&quot; They don't realize the magic that allows him to be bestowed with the ability and recognize that impossibility - they instead see the supernatural effect of him moving electricity with his mind, and think -that- is the impossible part.<br /> <br /> I could, in theory, grant a stage magician +5 Subterfuge (or bonuses to whatever is required for stage magic). This stage magician could go into this same area, perform these tricks and convince everyone who sees it that it is clearly, obviously, magic - but though people would rationalize it, it would not cause Dissonance because even though the Sleepers perceive a 'clearly' supernatural event, it's not the spell they are seeing. It's a form of slight of hand in both cases.<br /> <br /> Now I understand that in this example, the stage magician isn't using anything supernatural at all - that's part of my case though. The Sleepers in both cases are not looking at the spell - they are not looking at the magic that enhanced or bestowed these skills to these targets. They are looking at the subject, and what they do when those effects are on them. In my opinion, Dissonance has as much an effect on a non-supernal supernatural quality granted to a to subect as it does to a non-supernal -anything- granted to the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1091960-dissonance-edge-cases?p=1093116#post1093116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the problem <i>here</i> is that the Sleepwalker's friends are under no compulsion to believe him and Dissonance does not &quot;target&quot; mages directly. A rat with gills challenges &quot;rats don't have gills&quot; rather than &quot;you cannot give mammals the features of fish&quot; and liquid diamonds challenge &quot;diamonds are not liquid at room temperature&quot; rather than &quot;you can't cold-melt diamonds.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right - they don't target the mage directly; But in this case they aren't. They are targeting the spell of the mage. If the spell of a mage causes a rat to breath underwater, it will be challenged as 'rat's don't breath underwater'. However, if the spell of the mage gives the rat's owner the capability of turning the rat into a rat with gills with a cool supernatural merit, the rat with gills is not going to be subject to the dissonance - the supernal effect is that you -can- give mammals the features of fish, and they are too busy challenging than 'rats don't have gills'.<br /> <br /> In this scenario, the -only- valid target of Dissonance is the Forge Destiny spell. The Electrokinesis is not, because it is not supernal - the use of the merit involves no spell, no magic for the purposes of the Awakened perception. Like your rat, people do not challenge &quot;You cannot give people the ability to use Electrokinesis&quot;. I'd argue they don't even challenge &quot;People don't have Electrokinesis&quot;. They challenge &quot;You cannot control electricity with your mind&quot;.<br /> <br /> Put another way, they do not challenge what the Sleepwalker <i>has.</i> They challenge what the Sleepwalker is <i>doing. </i><br /> <br /> Finally, though its also a bit off topic - I feel like if you did this - gave a Sleepwalker the ability to cause this much mayhem and get people looking into the supernatural - that it would most definitely qualify as a breach - you are exposing the Sleeper Culture to the Mysteries through your lack of foresight into that sleepwalkers character. It may not be -Supernal- Mysteries, but it definately qualifies; I mean heck, just so much as getting an investigation going in the general area of a mage is enough to be a breach - getting the town square crying 'witch' at your Sleepwalker &quot;friend&quot; is not going to get any brownie points *G*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1513,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","user":"Jakondite","date":".  Grammar / Spelling 05-16-2017, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}